From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Data Exchange, XCAF - read the datum point from its own array,
 not the annotation plane's

XCAFDoc_Datum::GetObject builds the datum's point from aLoc, the array the
ChildLab_PlaneLoc block above it fills, instead of aPnt, the point's own:

  gp_Pnt aP(aLoc->Value(aPnt->Lower()),
            aPnt->Value(aPnt->Lower() + 1),
            aPnt->Value(aPnt->Lower() + 2));

The sibling block in XCAFDoc_GeomTolerance::GetObject is otherwise identical
and reads aPnt->Value(aPnt->Lower()), so this is a one-character divergence
rather than a shared idiom.

Two consequences.

A wrong answer when the datum has both. Measured: a datum written with plane
location (6,6,6) and point (7,7,7) reads back with point (6,7,7). The stored
point is not recoverable from the returned object.

A null handle dereference when the datum has a point and no plane. aLoc is
declared before the plane block and assigned only by a successful
FindAttribute there, so it is still null when the point block runs. Measured:
SIGSEGV, both in the process that wrote the datum and after saving the same
document to BinXCAF and reloading it into a fresh TDocStd_Application, so the
crashing shape survives persistence and any reader of such a file meets it.
XCAFDimTolObjects_DatumObject's HasPlane and HasPoint are independent flags and
XCAFDoc_Datum::SetObject writes the two blocks independently, so a
point-without-plane datum is what the public API produces for that object.

Fix: read the point's own array. Three GTests in the existing
XCAFDoc_GDT_Test.cxx cover the value with both present, the crash with a point
and no plane, and a plane with no point as the control, that last being the
shape STEPCAFControl_Reader produces (it sets a datum plane and never a datum
point).

SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#1022.
---
 src/DataExchange/TKXCAF/XCAFDoc/XCAFDoc_Datum.cxx | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/DataExchange/TKXCAF/XCAFDoc/XCAFDoc_Datum.cxx b/src/DataExchange/TKXCAF/XCAFDoc/XCAFDoc_Datum.cxx
index ca4abc714..4b39ca810 100644
--- a/src/DataExchange/TKXCAF/XCAFDoc/XCAFDoc_Datum.cxx
+++ b/src/DataExchange/TKXCAF/XCAFDoc/XCAFDoc_Datum.cxx
@@ -436,7 +436,8 @@ occ::handle<XCAFDimTolObjects_DatumObject> XCAFDoc_Datum::GetObject() const
   if (Label().FindChild(ChildLab_Pnt).FindAttribute(TDataStd_RealArray::GetID(), aPnt)
       && aPnt->Length() == 3)
   {
-    gp_Pnt aP(aLoc->Value(aPnt->Lower()),
+    // aLoc is the annotation plane's array and is null without a plane; read the point's own.
+    gp_Pnt aP(aPnt->Value(aPnt->Lower()),
               aPnt->Value(aPnt->Lower() + 1),
               aPnt->Value(aPnt->Lower() + 2));
     anObj->SetPoint(aP);
